This is the documentation for the function tf.required_space_to_batch_paddings:

"tf.required_space_to_batch_paddings(input_shape, block_shape, base_paddings=None, name=None)
Calculate padding required to make block_shape divide input_shape.

  This function can be used to calculate a suitable paddings argument for use
  with space_to_batch_nd and batch_to_space_nd.

  Args:
    input_shape: int32 Tensor of shape [N].
    block_shape: int32 Tensor of shape [N].
    base_paddings: Optional int32 Tensor of shape [N, 2].  Specifies the minimum
      amount of padding to use.  All elements must be >= 0.  If not specified,
      defaults to 0.
    name: string.  Optional name prefix.

  Returns:
    (paddings, crops), where:

    `paddings` and `crops` are int32 Tensors of rank 2 and shape [N, 2]
    satisfying:

        paddings[i, 0] = base_paddings[i, 0].
        0 <= paddings[i, 1] - base_paddings[i, 1] < block_shape[i]
        (input_shape[i] + paddings[i, 0] + paddings[i, 1]) % block_shape[i] == 0

        crops[i, 0] = 0
        crops[i, 1] = paddings[i, 1] - base_paddings[i, 1]

  Raises: ValueError if called with incompatible shapes.
  "

